      "block": {
        "type": "text",
        "label": "READ ALOUD · THE CHICKEN THIEF",
        "html": "<i>Read the story aloud. Slowly first, then a second time a little faster. The teacher marks the words to practise.</i><br><br>Lucas is twelve years old and he lives in the city. Every July, he spends his holidays at his grandma Rosa's farm. Grandma has two cows, a horse and twelve chickens. Every morning, Lucas feeds the chickens and collects the eggs from the henhouse.<br><br>Last July, something strange happened. On Monday morning, while Lucas was collecting the eggs, he noticed that one chicken was missing. There were white feathers on the ground near the fence.<br><br>\"Maybe she escaped,\" said Grandma.<br><br>But on Wednesday, another chicken disappeared. Grandma was worried. \"If this continues, we won't have any eggs!\" she said.<br><br>Lucas decided to investigate. Near the fence, he found some small footprints in the mud. They had four toes and long claws.<br><br>\"These aren't dog footprints,\" Grandma said. \"Our dog has bigger paws.\"<br><br>That night, Lucas couldn't sleep. At midnight, he was looking out of his bedroom window when he saw something near the henhouse. It had orange fur, pointed ears and a long, bushy tail. It was a fox! The fox was digging a hole under the fence.<br><br>Lucas ran to Grandma's room. While they were running outside, the fox escaped into the woods.<br><br>The next day, they repaired the fence and bought a new lock for the henhouse.<br><br>\"If foxes are hungry, they look for easy food,\" Grandma explained. \"So we must lock the henhouse every night. If we do that, the fox won't come back.\"<br><br>Now it's July again. Lucas is staying at the farm, and the chickens are safe. Every evening, he checks the lock. Right now, he is sitting on the porch with his notebook. He is writing a new story called \"Lucas, the Farm Detective.\""
      }
    },
